WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.260
Blue holes are normally
found on reefs.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.990
Yet this wouldn't be the
first time a chasm has

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:08.480
opened up close to
Australia's east coast.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.470
In September 2015, a
giant hole appears

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:15.350
overnight at a campsite
on Inskip Point,

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.380
swallowing a 1000 foot
long section of

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.330
coastline, cars and
caravans.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.960
A fear made all the more
real by a recent

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.240
scientific expedition
close to the Great

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.260
Barrier Reef.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.200
Researchers have recently
discovered an area where

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.800
part of the reef is
actually breaking away

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.890
and is perched above a
deep underwater canyon.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:43.880
The giant disintegrating
slab is one and a half

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:44.990
miles long.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.310
It's only a matter of
time that this will

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:53.120
eventually tumble down
and will create a tsunami

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.130
that could be absolutely
catastrophic.

